From: OmacVM
Subject: [PATCH] audio: the sound thread's tick follows the streams

What: on the sound's own thread (qemu-audio-own-thread.patch,
OMACVM_AUDIO_THREAD=1) each tick says the longest period it can take, and
the thread runs at the shortest of them, 1-10 ms, instead of every 1 ms:
- an HDA stream: a quarter of the guest's shortest DMA entry (the guest's
  periods; it sees its position move once a tick), at most an eighth of the
  codec's 8 KiB buffer, which one tick fills or drains;
- the mixer: a quarter of QEMU's ring minus two of the backend's buffers
  (one for CoreAudio's next callback, one in flight), read every tick, so a
  reopen with bigger buffers (AirPods, #548) shortens the tick at once. The
  SDL backend says its open device's size (HWVoiceOut/In.omacvm_frames).
A tick that does not know counts as 1 ms. The guest's usual 1024-frame
periods and the own thread's 256-frame CoreAudio buffers give 5.33 ms:
about 190 wakeups a second instead of 1000. The HDA pacing burst grows with
the period (a period plus the 4.3 ms of slack a late tick had at 1 ms), so
a regular tick is never taken for a stall. The thread re-sets its
time-constraint policy for a new period and logs "OmacVM: sound: audio tick
every <N> us"; the start line ("own audio thread, <policy>, every <N> us")
is unchanged. OMACVM_AUDIO_THREAD_PERIOD_US still fixes the period (250-10000;
1000 = before this patch).

Why: a real-time thread waking 1000 times a second keeps the Mac's cores out
of idle while any stream is open, silence too. MacBook Air M2, a browser
blend with a video playing: the sound path 0.32 W, a fixed 4 ms tick -0.09 W
(work/power-1116/attrib.md). A fixed longer tick is not safe: at 5.33 ms the
pacing's 5.33 ms burst forgave every tick as a stall (the guest's clock ran
slow), and with AirPods' 1024-frame buffers QEMU's 32 ms ring has no room
for it. Following the streams keeps every buffer's margin where it is tight
and the queued audio (latency) as before.

Applies after qemu-audio-own-thread.patch and the SDL audio patches.
Upstream: not sent (OmacVM only, like the own thread).
Test: src/tests/audio-timing.sh checks the wiring; app/runtime/Tests/audio
(glitches.py, sdlprobe loopback round trip) and work/power-1116/snd have the
runs (glitches, round trip, the Air's whole-machine A/B).

diff --git a/audio/audio-mixeng-be.c b/audio/audio-mixeng-be.c
index c87c412..e00b2fe 100644
--- a/audio/audio-mixeng-be.c
+++ b/audio/audio-mixeng-be.c
@@ -588,11 +588,58 @@ static int audio_is_timer_needed(AudioMixengBackend *s)
 
 static void audio_rt_timer(void *opaque);
 
+/*
+ * OmacVM (qemu-audio-tick-follows-stream.patch): the longest tick a voice's
+ * ring can take. The ring keeps one backend buffer for the next callback and
+ * one in flight; the tick may use a quarter of the rest, so a late tick still
+ * has three quarters. 0: not known, or the ring is tight already (1 ms).
+ */
+static int64_t audio_rt_ring_period(size_t ring, int frames, int freq)
+{
+    if (frames <= 0 || freq <= 0 || ring <= 2 * (size_t)frames) {
+        return 0;
+    }
+    return muldiv64((ring - 2 * (size_t)frames) / 4, NANOSECONDS_PER_SECOND,
+                    freq);
+}
+
+/* The shortest of the enabled voices (audio lock held). */
+static int64_t audio_rt_mixer_period(AudioMixengBackend *s)
+{
+    HWVoiceOut *hwo;
+    HWVoiceIn *hwi;
+    int64_t p, m = -1;
+
+    QLIST_FOREACH(hwo, &s->hw_head_out, entries) {
+        if (hwo->enabled) {
+            p = audio_rt_ring_period(hwo->samples,
+                                     qatomic_read(&hwo->omacvm_frames),
+                                     hwo->info.freq);
+            m = m < 0 ? p : MIN(m, p);
+        }
+    }
+    QLIST_FOREACH(hwi, &s->hw_head_in, entries) {
+        if (hwi->enabled) {
+            p = audio_rt_ring_period(hwi->samples,
+                                     qatomic_read(&hwi->omacvm_frames),
+                                     hwi->info.freq);
+            m = m < 0 ? p : MIN(m, p);
+        }
+    }
+    return m < 0 ? 0 : m;
+}
+
 static void audio_reset_timer(AudioMixengBackend *s)
 {
     if (audio_is_timer_needed(s)) {
         if (audio_rt_enabled()) {
-            /* OmacVM: on the sound's own thread, every audio_rt_period(). */
+            /*
+             * OmacVM: on the sound's own thread, every audio_rt_period().
+             * Each tick comes here: a reopened Mac output (AirPods: bigger
+             * buffers) counts at once.
+             */
+            audio_rt_tick_set_max_period(&s->rt_tick,
+                                         audio_rt_mixer_period(s));
             audio_rt_tick_add(&s->rt_tick, audio_rt_timer, s);
         } else {
             timer_mod_anticipate_ns(s->ts,
@@ -635,6 +682,7 @@ static void audio_rt_timer(void *opaque)
     int64_t now, diff;
     AudioMixengBackend *s = opaque;
 
+
     now = qemu_clock_get_ns(QEMU_CLOCK_VIRTUAL);
     diff = now - s->timer_last;
     if (diff > audio_rt_period() * 3 / 2) {
